# Architecture

## Layers

- `app/` — routing only. Pages are thin: fetch via queries, render feature UI.
- `features/<name>/` — domain modules (`components`, `types`, `data`, `queries`, optional `actions`).
- `components/ui` — shadcn primitives only.
- `components/layout` — SiteShell, Sidebar, Topbar, StatusBar.
- `components/shared` — Pane, SectionLabel, CmdButton, MediaPlaceholder, Tag.
- `server/db`, `server/services`, `server/validators` — backend.
- `lib/site.ts` — static site content (copy, nav, experience, stack, contact).
- `lib/` — utils, constants, shared helpers.
- `hooks/` — shared client hooks.

## Design system

- Dark, readable portfolio: Space Grotesk (headings) + IBM Plex Mono (small labels).
- Present content as headings, cards, timelines, and tags — not fake terminal or code dumps.
- Tokens live in `app/globals.css` (`--background`, `--accent` teal `#1fe0b8`, etc.).
- Prefer shared components over one-off section styles when repeating patterns.

## Add something new

**New page:** `app/(site)/<route>/page.tsx` + optional `features/<name>/` + nav in `lib/site.ts` if needed.

**New home section:** `features/<name>/components/*-section.tsx` + mount in `app/(site)/page.tsx` + `NAV_SECTIONS` entry.

**New feature without page (widget/popup):** `features/<name>/` + mount once in `SiteShell` / site layout.

**New API:** `app/api/<resource>/route.ts` → call `server/services/`.

**Chat:** global popup under `features/chat/`, never a `/chat` page unless explicitly requested.

## Do not

- Put business logic or DB calls in `page.tsx`.
- Put feature-specific UI in `components/ui`.
- Create empty routes for unknown future pages.
